program            = 002_string_literal_handling
area               = 11_literals_and_strings
description        = String literal concatenation across adjacent and multi-line forms, individual element access, embedded and terminating nulls
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- NO STRING LITERAL IS EVER MODIFIED. Modifying a string literal is undefined
  behaviour. Every aggregate in this program is declared static const char[] and
  initialized from string literals as C11 6.7.9p14 permits, and the two literals
  indexed directly are only read. No pointer to any literal is ever written through,
  and literal_length takes a const char * parameter.
- No signed integer overflow. Every printed value is either a small array size cast
  to int, a length counter bounded by a short array, or an unsigned char element
  (range 0..255) widened to int.
- No shift operations of any kind, so no shift count can be out of range.
- No out-of-bounds access. The loops over concatenated, across_lines and with_escapes
  stop before the terminator, and the terminator of concatenated, of across_lines and
  of the hello literal is then read on its own at index sizeof - 1, the last element
  of the array. The loop over embedded_nul covers the whole array, so that both the
  interior null and the terminating null are read, which is also within the array.
  literal_length stops at the first null byte, which every array contains. No
  one-past-end pointer is dereferenced.
- No aliasing violation. Each array is declared char and each element is read and
  converted through unsigned char, which is always permitted.
- No uninitialized read. Every array has a static const initializer; zero has a
  static initializer; the counter n in literal_length is initialized before use.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points. At most one argument of any
  call reads the volatile object zero, so no access to it is unsequenced with another
  access to it. Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the addresses of unrelated
  objects, and no address or pointer value is printed.
- Verified empirically: the default strict warning gate (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic
  -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero diagnostics, and
  -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all runs to completion with no
  output and exit status 0.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Plain char is never printed directly. Every character element is converted through
unsigned char before being widened to int, so the measured plain-char signedness
difference (plain char is signed on x86_64 and i686 but unsigned on aarch64 and
riscv64) cannot be observed in this program's output. Handled by construction, not by
a marker.

Only int-typed values are printed, always with %d. No long, no size_t and no pointer
is printed, so the measured i686 width difference (sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *)
are 4 on i686 and 8 on the other three targets) has no effect. The sizeof results
that are printed are sizes of char arrays, which are counts of bytes with
sizeof(char) fixed at 1 on every target, and each is cast to int before printing.

Every character in every literal is a printable US-ASCII character or a control
character below 128, so no execution-character-set difference can arise. The one
control character among them, the tab in with_escapes, is reported as its decimal
value rather than emitted literally, so the golden record below is printable ASCII
throughout.

String literal concatenation, element access and null termination were measured
byte-identical across all four targets at every optimization level, so this program
is fully cross-comparable and all three oracles are enabled.
END
